# Top-level Python libraries for the typed document tools (issue #24).
#
# The runtime image installs exactly `requirements.lock`, never this file baked
# from the index: the lock is the resolved, fully pinned set. Keep the two in
# step; `packages/python-tool/test/lock.test.ts` fails when a name here is
# missing from the lock or the lock carries an unpinned line.
#
# markitdown is deliberately absent. Measured on the Alpine 3.24.4 base it pulls
# a conversion stack of its own on top of these five libraries (see
# docs/implementation/14-deployment.md) and would consume most of the 400 MB
# image budget to re-read the three formats this set already reads directly.
# read_document produces Markdown from python-docx, openpyxl and pypdf.
#
# pandas is absent: no tool in this slice aggregates data frames.
# pandoc is absent: the binary is large and the PDF path is reportlab, not
# DOCX->Markdown.
python-docx==1.2.0
openpyxl==3.1.5
pypdf==7.1.1
reportlab==5.1.0
pillow==13.0.0
